<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48914" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θοάζω</span></b>  (B), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάασσω</span>
			, <i>sit</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοφίης ἐπ᾽ ἄκροισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					4.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπ᾽ ἀρχᾶς οὔτινος θοάζων [Ζεὺς]
					κρατύνει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					595
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίνας ποθ᾽ ἕδρας τάσδε μοι
				θοάζετε</span>; why <i>are ye in</i> this <i>suppliant
				posture?</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.22e
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιθοάζω, θόωκος,
			θῶκος</span>; 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάσσω</span>
			.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
